Core patch iam-role-transform-boundary (CP-431)

VAMS fork core patch for GitHub issue #431: the IamRoleTransform aspect
(infra/lib/aspects/iam-role-transform.aspect.ts) overrides PermissionsBoundary with
AWS::NoValue in both branches, so cdk.json environments.aws.PermissionBoundaryArn never
reaches a role and the CDK @aws-cdk/core:permissionsBoundary context is removed too. This
patch sets the boundary on every AWS::IAM::Role when the ARN is non-empty and leaves the
property alone when it is empty. It does not change the role naming (every role still gets
an explicit RoleName).

Made against VAMS v2.6.6. The development branch fixed #431 upstream on 2026-11-05 in a different
form, so on a fork based on it the patch neither applies nor reads as present: remove the entry there.
Activate: copy this file to <home>/ledger/core-patches/ and list it in core-patches.md
(see ledger-template/core-patches.md). vra build and vra iam plan apply it to their scratch
copy of the fork; vra build then checks that every role in the synthesized templates carries
the boundary. Retire the entry when upstream ships the fix (the engine reports the patch as
"present" once the fork already contains the change).

diff --git a/infra/lib/aspects/iam-role-transform.aspect.ts b/infra/lib/aspects/iam-role-transform.aspect.ts
--- a/infra/lib/aspects/iam-role-transform.aspect.ts
+++ b/infra/lib/aspects/iam-role-transform.aspect.ts
@@ -56,11 +56,20 @@ export class IamRoleTransform implements cdk.IAspect {
                     () => {},
                     this.ApplyOverride(node, "RoleName", this.getRoleName(node))
                 );
-                cdk.Fn.conditionIf(
-                    this.conditionBoundary.logicalId,
-                    this.ApplyOverride(node, "PermissionsBoundary", Aws.NO_VALUE),
-                    this.ApplyOverride(node, "PermissionsBoundary", Aws.NO_VALUE)
-                );
+                // Core patch iam-role-transform-boundary (GitHub issue #431): apply the boundary when it is
+                // set. A literal ARN (cdk.json environments.aws.PermissionBoundaryArn) is set as is; a token
+                // (the rolePrefix/permissionBoundaryArn parameters of RoleRename) is resolved by the
+                // conditionBoundary condition. An empty ARN leaves the property alone, so the CDK
+                // @aws-cdk/core:permissionsBoundary context still applies.
+                const boundary = this.permissionsBoundaryArn;
+                if (cdk.Token.isUnresolved(boundary)) {
+                    node.addPropertyOverride(
+                        "PermissionsBoundary",
+                        cdk.Fn.conditionIf(this.conditionBoundary.logicalId, Aws.NO_VALUE, boundary)
+                    );
+                } else if (boundary) {
+                    this.ApplyOverride(node, "PermissionsBoundary", boundary);
+                }
             }
         }
     }
